From c4834678ee40c671d7560af34d26a4f0c8f15a30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Developer <dev@example.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:10:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: don't spin forever when the Lean session is lost; stop
 image jitter

The proof state request swallowed every error and returned null, which the
proof panel shows as "loading", so a lost connection or an outdated RPC
session left players with an endless spinner and no feedback. The RPC
session was also never reconnected.

- Rethrow errors from Game.getProofState, with a 90 s timeout, and don't
  retry an outdated session (RpcNeedsReconnect, -32900).
- Drop an outdated RPC session so PlayableLevel connects a new one.
- Show a message with Retry and Reload buttons when the server can't be
  reached.
- Reserve the scrollbar's space in the proof panel and clip the spinner:
  the rotating spinner changed the scroll height, which toggled the
  scrollbar, which resized the world image, in a loop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
